findings.body:
The base class and v2 use the built-in generics `set[tuple[str, ...]]`. This override imports `Set` and `Tuple` from `typing`, which have been deprecated since Python 3.9. Ruff's `UP006`/`UP035` rules usually flag these in this repo.

::diff{file="api/core/workflow/nodes/variable_assigner/v1/node.py" lines="2-2"}

Revert the import to `from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any` and annotate the parameter as `set[tuple[str, ...]]` to match `Node.blocks_variable_output` in `api/core/workflow/nodes/base/node.py:435`.

In CLEAR mode, `updated_variable` is built from `{"value": income_value.to_object()}`. That means `updated_variable.to_object()` and `income_value.to_object()` return the same value, so the new branch does nothing:

::diff{file="api/core/workflow/nodes/variable_assigner/v1/node.py" lines="102-111"}

It adds lines that are unrelated to the streaming fix and makes the diff harder to read. Unless there's a behavior difference I'm missing, drop it and keep `"value": income_value.to_object()`.
